<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48185" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεοισεχθρία</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>hatefulness to the gods,
			villainy</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				22.59
			</span></i> (written <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεοῖς ἐχθρίαν</span>),
			prob. in <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>V.</u>
				418
			</span></i> (required by Cretic metre), in <i><span class="en">
				Archipp.
				35
			</span></i> (where the first two syll. coalesce), and in <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Lex.</u>
				11
			</span></i>: in the last three places codd. have <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεοσεχθρία</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεὸς ἐχθρία
				</span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεοσεχθρα</span>
			v.l.
			<i><span class="en">
				Archipp.
			</span></i> l.c.): <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεοεχθρία</span> is found
			in Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ra.</u>
				557
			</span></i>, v.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Lex.</u>
			</span></i>l.c.; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεοῖς ἐχθρός</span> in
				<i><span class="en">
				D.
				19.95
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				24.195
			</span></i>.</div>
